From 501e6e7ca9754d29e02edddfd5268718480a8dac Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 23:32:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] tools/dvbridge, settings: an SDR display of the user's own
 white and gamma

"Dolby Vision to SDR: the display it is made for" had three displays:
Reference (white at 203 cd/m2, BT.1886), Bright room (300, gamma 2.2) and
Projector (100). It now has a fourth, Custom, with the white (20 to 500
cd/m2) and the gamma (1.8 to 2.8, the pure powers that libplacebo has as an
SDR EOTF) set by the user at the expert level. The setting is named "HDR to
SDR" in the four languages: it always applied to HDR10, HDR10+ and HLG mapped
to SDR by the bridge as well, not only to Dolby Vision.

dvbridge_sdr_mapping_custom() makes the mapping; a white of 203 and a gamma
of 2.4 are the reference's mapping, bit for bit. Measured on Mesa's software
OpenGL ES (llvmpipe and zink): Custom at 203 and 2.4, 100 and 2.4, and 300
and 2.2 give the same bytes as Reference, Projector and Bright room; with
content that the display holds, the output of each gamma from 1.8 to 2.8 is
within 0.062 of a 10-bit code of the pure power computed exactly. The trim
pass of an SDR target reads its picture with the target's gamma.
