+
+#. Hades: label of setting "videoscreen.hadesdvsdrwhite"; translated in Estuary (#32616)
+#: system/settings/settings.xml
+msgctxt "#41136"
+msgid "Custom: white of the display"
+msgstr ""
+
+#. Hades: help of setting "videoscreen.hadesdvsdrwhite"; translated in Estuary (#32617)
+#: system/settings/settings.xml
+msgctxt "#41137"
+msgid "For \"Custom\": the white that your display shows in SDR, in nits (cd/m²), as measured or as its maker states it: about 100 for a projector or a display in a dark room, 200 to 300 for a TV in a lit room. The brighter the white, the lower the codes the picture is sent with, so that it keeps the brightness it was made for; the dimmer, the higher, and what is brighter than this white is compressed. 203 with gamma 2.4 is Reference, the same picture. Applies from the next video."
+msgstr ""
+
+#. Hades: label of setting "videoscreen.hadesdvsdrgamma"; translated in Estuary (#32618)
+#: system/settings/settings.xml
+msgctxt "#41138"
+msgid "Custom: gamma of the display"
